From a6d29da2e192592f1f2266ab22fa880f34b3134d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:17:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06905/11362] [outer-loop] re86: L8 SOLVED, FULL GAME CLEAR
 (round 7, codex)

Round-7 gpt-5.6-sol session confirmed round 6's own diagnosis: returned
to round 5's FULL per-fixture route (not the shortcut round 6 ruled
out) and it worked. Confirmed the load-bearing mechanic precisely: a
22x4 outline must be shifted LEFT to x=3..24 before descending from its
color swatch -- the tempting x=6..27 position is adjacency-unsafe,
silently repainting the neighboring swatch, which is exactly what
caused round 6's null.

Applied that one-step safety shift to both the color-11 and color-6
rectangles via the shared corridor and palette-wall opening, placing
both target geometries simultaneously. levels_completed advanced 7->8
on action 689 of a 689-action sequence.

Independently re-verified by the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() +
replay via a new resolver priority branch (dict-shaped labels,
JSON-normalized), all 5 confirmed level=8, state=GameState.WIN -- L8
is the FINAL level. The game is fully solved.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: re86 levels_reproduced 7 -> 8,
full_game_clear: true, final_game_state: GameState.WIN.
reproducible_total_levels 162 -> 163 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
